   I think I might as well throw in my two cents worth again:
 
     1)  Traps/polypiles:   I am sure someone already suggested this,
  but I'll do it again, just to reinforce the idea. . .   When you
  polymorph a pile, things should get a little screwed up, sure, but
  just like polymorphing yourself, there should be a chance of system
  shock.  Whatever the chance may be (perhaps with higher powered items
  having a less chance of blowing up, but rocks having a huge chance of
  blowing up, etc. . . ) there should be some ramification to their
  destruction, not simply "poof" there gone.  What if all "poofed" items
  turn into some kind of trap?  therefor, polypiling a HUGE pile would
  cause one little square to have, possibly, dozens of traps (I don't
  think this should be toooo hard to code, but I could be wrong)
 
      2) Addendum:  What if polymorphing a pile also could create a
  POLYMONSTER, you know from all those bugs on the ground you watch when
  you engrave?   This thing, for a thing it is, would change type each move
  just like hallucination, of course, it would actually BE all those monsters.
  The hit points, however, would be equall to the power level of the items
  that went poof.
 
      3) Addendum Addendum:  Is there any penalty for killing an untamed
   pet?  What about geneociding your own pet-species?  Just wondering.


